1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
He lent people five hundred bucks, then took back almost two grand.

2
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:07,231
The paperwork said six fifty. So where'd the rest come from?

3
00:00:08,081 --> 00:00:11,165
Scott Tucker. Online payday loans. Here's the— here's the trick.

4
00:00:12,015 --> 00:00:14,053
Hit like if you've ever signed without reading.

5
00:00:14,353 --> 00:00:18,502
Every payday, the loan renewed by default. He'd pull a hundred fifty in fees…

6
00:00:19,352 --> 00:00:21,252
And the five hundred you owed? Didn't move.

7
00:00:21,552 --> 00:00:25,842
The Justice Department described one borrower who paid fourteen twenty-five in fees.

8
00:00:26,142 --> 00:00:28,829
Send this to the friend who says it's just a small fee.

9
00:00:29,729 --> 00:00:32,011
One of at least four and a half million borrowers.

10
00:00:32,911 --> 00:00:35,532
A jury convicted him on all fourteen counts.

11
00:00:35,832 --> 00:00:39,280
The sentence? Follow first, 'cause this page reads the fine print for you.

12
00:00:39,730 --> 00:00:43,300
Two hundred months. That's over sixteen years.

13
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:47,191
So if the fee never touches the five hundred… what's it for?
